    "text": "Two satellites&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> are revolving round the earth at height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math> are the time periods of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math> :<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/431cc50f-c163-4ae7-84da-5394019bf440-image.png\" style=\"width: 196px; height: 180px;\" /></p><p>[ Given : radius of earth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;mass of earth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>24</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> ]</p>",
